title scooter_paint -- a live status bar in colour
prompt take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the recursion loop; deep-read one council-rota doc; send often; stop at custody gates
think Read REMEMBER's INNER LOOP live edge, the 1024-round itinerary, the eight-season double-seat, and the Rye-first crypto wave for the road. The live edge is Season G open media -- the terminal-meets-pixels family. The prior lap gave image/text_grid.rye its per-cell BACKGROUND (render_grid_cells / paint_grid_cells -- the full coloured terminal cell in the abstract). The pattern is clear: abstract rung in image/, then the same capability made LIVE in pond/apps.
think The lap before THAT brought text_grid's per-cell FOREGROUND live into scooter_paint (render_channel_fg -- a coloured header word). So the natural next Lindy-first crux is to bring per-cell BACKGROUND live: render_channel_bar -- a real coloured STATUS BAR, the header ink over its own header GROUND band, exactly the parallel move. Floor code that does not wait on paused Brushstroke; every glass surface will paint a status bar.
think Method, witness-first: paint_frame_cells is the two-palette sibling of paint_frame_fg (same paintability guard); render_channel_bar builds an in-header fg/bg palette and passes through to text_grid.render_grid_cells. Green looks like: byte-for-byte the same as text_grid painting from the same cells; walking row 0 no pixel stays white and blue shows between glyphs; the body region byte-for-byte identical to the single-ink face; round-trips through QOI; a mis-sized bg refuses GridBgMismatch by name.
obs A real red, met with standfast (root not symptom): first I chose WHITE header ink over blue, so the header glyph pixels were legitimately white and tripped the walk-row-0 "no pixel stays white" assert. text_grid's own bar proof uses a non-white ink (red) on blue for exactly this reason. Fixed to YELLOW ink -- distinct from both the white page and the blue ground -- a real bright-on-blue status bar, and the measure reads clean.
obs A second red, a copy slip: the determinism check re-rendered bar2 with a WHITE header ink where bar used YELLOW, and same_bytes rightly refused -- the guard caught the slip. Fixed bar2 to yellow so the twin proves beside the elder. Pinpointed by converting asserts to distinct error returns and adding trace prints, then removed all scaffolding before GREEN.
obs Body-untouched proof strengthened from a fragile single-pixel check (which depended on glyph (1,0) inking pixel 0,0 -- and '[' does) to a robust whole-region byte-for-byte equality against the single-ink face; the colouring is confined to the status row.
obs Correctly layered -- pond composes image, never the reverse; no new symlinks (render_grid_cells lives in the already-linked text_grid.rye). No network, no key, no funds; the wire between two Constel piers reaches the serve gate, the maintainer's hand.
